    "body": "## Parent\n\n#172\n\n## What to build\n\nCompose module-owned Tasks, Action Items, connectors, and Weekly Summary runtimes; expose five-area navigation; wire startup synchronization and weekly scheduling; and prove the real Shell production composition.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Production navigation exposes Content Engine, Content Research, Person Profiles, Meeting Wizard, and Tasks.\n- [ ] The Tasks module owns Task stores, Action Item promotion, and connector semantics behind its application interface.\n- [ ] Meeting Debrief produces Action Items and Gmail drafts without owning promoted Tasks or provider receipts.\n- [ ] Meeting Wizard reads bounded projections for Today and This week without owning source records.\n- [ ] The Shell holds Workspace handles, ordering, credentials, and route registration while module composition owns internal stores and adapters.\n- [ ] Real production composition wires startup synchronization, weekly generation, and weekly email scheduling.\n- [ ] A Shell composition test proves every runtime is reachable with production adapters rather than test-only wiring.\n- [ ] `npm run check` is green.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #168 — Deepen the Meeting Brief Generator behind one enrichment seam\n- #181 — Automatically create confirmed owner Tasks\n- #187 — Retry, poll, unlink, and delete Google-linked Tasks\n- #191 — Resolve Asana drift and completion conflicts\n- #193 — Promote the clean Meeting Wizard Today experience\n- #197 — Send one owner Weekly Briefing email each Monday\n- #198 — Default BYOK onboarding to OpenRouter and Mercury\n- #199 — Retire positional Action Item state and bulk Google Task writes",
